rink":0.11371147037911533,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.2583764625802439,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02722,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"4D Molecular Therapeutics, Inc., a late-stage biotechnology company, engages in the development of adeno-associated virus vectors from its proprietary synthetic vector discovery platform, Therapeutic Vector Evolution in the Netherlands and the United States. The company's lead product candidate is 4D-150 for the treatment of retinal vascular diseases by providing multi-year sustained production of anti-VEGF from the retina with intravitreal injection, as well as for treating wet age-related macular degeneration and diabetic macular edema. It is also developing 4D-710, which is in early-stage study for the treatment of cystic fibrosis; 4D-175 that is in preclinical stage for treating geographic atrophy; and 4D-725, which is in preclinical stage for the treatment of alpha-1 anti-trypsin deficiency lung disease. 4D Molecular Therapeutics, Inc. has collaboration and licensing agreements with Otsuka Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd. The company was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in EmeryVille, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. David H. Kirn M.D. | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 196 people. Revenue per employee of $435K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 44%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $112K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["4D Molecular Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $677M market cap on $85M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +201% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -302% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $110M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 26% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (23.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 188% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 110% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"4D Molecular Therapeutics (FDMT) Projected to Release Quarterly Earnings on Tuesday","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/4d-molecular-therapeutics-fdmt-projected-to-release-quarterly-earnings-on-tuesday.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793726817.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Head to Head Analysis: Neurogene (NASDAQ:NGNE) & 4D Molecular Therapeutics (NASDAQ:FDMT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/head-to-head-analysis-neurogene-nasdaqngne-4d-molecular-therapeutics-nasdaqfdmt.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793702720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Contrasting 4D Molecular Therapeutics (NASDAQ:FDMT) & Oncocyte (NASDAQ:IMDX)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/contrasting-4d-molecular-therapeutics-nasdaqfd